ingredients:
  - "3/4 cup semolina"
  - "1 medium onion (chopped)"
  - "2 tsp oil"
  - "5 French beans (chopped)"
  - "1 small capsicum (chopped)"
  - "1/2 small cabbage (chopped)"
  - "1 small carrot (chopped)"
  - "2 dsp groundnuts"
  - "1 tsp sprouted green gram dal"
  - "1 tsp urad dal"
  - "2 green chilies (chopped)"
  - "1/2 tsp mustard seeds"
  - "Few curry leaves"
  - "3/4 cup water"
  - "Salt to taste"
instructions:
  - "Soak dal for 2 hours and drain the water."
  - "Chop all vegetables."
  - "Heat 2 tbsp oil, fry groundnuts and semolina separately, then set aside."
  - "Heat remaining oil, add mustard seeds, dals, and sauté onions until golden brown."
  - "Add chopped vegetables and sauté for a few minutes until tender."
  - "Mix in semolina, salt, and pour water, cooking until moisture evaporates and semolina is cooked."
  - "Garnish with groundnuts and chopped coriander leaves."
  - "Serve hot."
